  "reason": "The strongest evidence is config_018, where multimodal multiprofile PCA+ResNet with avgpool and concat reaches 0.619 accuracy and 0.610 F1, suggesting multiprofile aggregation is highly promising. However, only avgpool has been tested in this setting, leaving uncertainty about whether a more expressive aggregation could improve performance. config_020 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the same profile setting, encoders, and concat fusion, so it isolates the effect of aggregation. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the current best direction while testing an important unexplored design choice before moving to new encoders or other factors."
}

